                <pb facs="0422" n="410" xml:id="pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8830/2310: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-04-03T00:00:00-03:00">April 3,
                        1943—midnight.</date><lb/>[Received April 3—3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>727. Embassy deeply appreciates arrangements made regarding newsprint for
                    importers. <hi rendition="#italic">El Mundo</hi> situation is precarious still
                    and it is alleging discrimination on the part Argentine shipping lines.</p>
                <p>For the Department’s information in case it is approached Embassy is advising all
                    papers that cooperation among themselves would permit of more orderly flow of
                    supplies and avoidance of the many misunderstandings which have arisen in the
                    past.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
